GAL22V10
C68CPUVIDEO

; Processor U7 variant for systems with the video board installed.
; Physical /BANK_SEL pin remains high impedance; the video board drives it.
PHI2 RW VMA A15 A14 A13 A12 A11 A10 A9 A8 GND
NC NC NC NC NC NC BUSOK IOSELN BANKSELN ROMSELN RAMSELN VCC

BUSOK = PHI2 * VMA
RAMSELN = /PHI2 + /VMA + A15 * A14

; GALasm requires a tristate output expression before its enable term.
; PHI2 * /PHI2 is always false, so pin 21 never drives /BANK_SEL.
BANKSELN.T = PHI2
BANKSELN.E = PHI2 * /PHI2

IOSELN = /PHI2 + /VMA + /A15 + /A14 + /A13 + A12 + A11 + A10 + A9 + A8
ROMSELN = /PHI2 + /VMA + /A15 + /A14 + /A13 + /A12 * /A11 * /A10 * /A9 * /A8

DESCRIPTION
C68 processor decoder for use with the video board. Pin 21 /BANK_SEL is
always high impedance. The video GAL generates /BANK_SEL or selects VRAM.
